  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "The University of Bradford is a public research university in Bradford, West Yorkshire. Founded in 1966, the university is best known for the School of Management (Triple Crown — AACSB, EQUIS, AMBA — top 1% globally), Faculty of Engineering and Informatics, the world-renowned Department of Peace Studies and International Development (the first in the world), Pharmacy, and Nursing. Bradford is a small, focused city-centre campus, one of the most ethnically diverse universities in the UK.",
      "International students enter via Oxford International pathway programmes — International Foundation, International Year One, and Pre-Master courses lead into a Bradford Bachelor's or Master's degree."
    ],
